<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:04:55 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>两千多年前，朱利叶斯·凯撒征服了最终成为巴黎的定居点。考古学家可能刚刚发现它</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-thousand-years-ago-julius-caesar-conquered-the-settlement-that-eventually-became-paris-archaeologists-may-have-just-found-it-180989569/</link><description>在塞纳河西岱岛的一家医院进行挖掘时，研究人员发现了可能曾经保护过卢泰西亚（法国首都的高卢前身）的城墙的一部分</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-thousand-years-ago-julius-caesar-conquered-the-settlement-that-eventually-became-paris-archaeologists-may-have-just-found-it-180989569/</guid></item><item><title>蝙蝠起源于哪里？大规模的基因研究可能解决了长期存在的争论并改写了生物的进化树</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-did-bats-originate-huge-genetic-study-may-have-settled-the-longstanding-debate-and-rewritten-the-creatures-evolutionary-tree-180989568/</link><description>根据这项新研究，飞行哺乳动物可能出现在 6500 万年前的欧洲，然后传播到非洲，然后传播到世界其他地方</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-did-bats-originate-huge-genetic-study-may-have-settled-the-longstanding-debate-and-rewritten-the-creatures-evolutionary-tree-180989568/</guid></item><item><title>参观刚刚归还希腊的一系列令人惊叹的被盗希腊文物，跨越 5000 年历史</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-a-stunning-collection-of-stolen-greek-artifacts-spanning-5000-years-that-were-just-returned-to-greece-180989566/</link><description>曼哈顿地区检察官小阿尔文·布拉格 (Alvin L. Bragg Jr.) 办公室的调查人员在大都会艺术博物馆没收了这些古董。</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-a-stunning-collection-of-stolen-greek-artifacts-spanning-5000-years-that-were-just-returned-to-greece-180989566/</guid></item><item><title>有些鸟鸣声比其他鸟鸣声更悦耳。对我们来说，更高音调、复杂的声音往往听起来更美妙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/some-birdsongs-are-more-pleasing-to-human-ears-than-others-higher-pitched-complex-calls-tend-to-sound-more-beautiful-to-us-180989540/</link><description>在一项新研究中，超过 80 名参与者对 123 种欧洲鸟类发出的声音的悦耳程度进行了评分。然后研究人员研究了最受欢迎和最不受欢迎的歌曲的音质</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:01:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/some-birdsongs-are-more-pleasing-to-human-ears-than-others-higher-pitched-complex-calls-tend-to-sound-more-beautiful-to-us-180989540/</guid></item><item><title>在古埃及堡垒中发现了拥有 3000 年历史的战马墓葬和拉美西斯二世石碑等文物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-3000-year-old-warhorse-burial-and-a-ramses-ii-tablet-among-other-relics-have-been-discovered-in-an-ancient-egyptian-fortress-180989564/</link><description>尼罗河三角洲的新发掘提供了有关新王国时代军事和居住生活的令人大开眼界的线索</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:07:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-3000-year-old-warhorse-burial-and-a-ramses-ii-tablet-among-other-relics-have-been-discovered-in-an-ancient-egyptian-fortress-180989564/</guid></item><item><title>为什么克劳德·莫奈一遍又一遍地画同样的场景？这位印象派艺术家痴迷于捕捉时间的转瞬即逝的本质</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</link><description>泰特现代美术馆即将举办的展览将展出莫奈在 1870 年代至 1920 年代创作的 60 多件艺术作品。这些作品揭示了他如何记录不断变化的光线和天气条件</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:01:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</guid></item><item><title>科学家表示，“超级”厄尔尼诺现象带来的酷热天气可能会在二月份导致近50万人死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</link><description>预测数字包括六月以来的死亡人数，可能低估了总死亡人数。炎热天气可能会持续到二月之后，气候变化可能会带来其他危及生命的情况，包括洪水、野火和传染病</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</guid></item><item><title>一位金属探测器在德国勘探时惊讶地发现了大量罗马硬币</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</link><description>943 枚第纳尔银币跨越了从公元前 148 年到公元 124 或 125 年近 300 年的罗马历史</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</guid></item><item><title>这幅来源神秘的立体派绘画在芝加哥艺术博物馆悬挂了数十年。现在，博物馆将把它归还给合法的犹太继承人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</link><description>红外成像将 20 世纪 Jean Metzinger 的作品与一位收藏家联系起来，该收藏家的作品在二战期间被纳粹命令强制拍卖</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:18:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</guid></item><item><title>土耳其研究人员出土了一块刻有世界上最古老和平条约的古代碎片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</link><description>这块泥板上刻有阿卡德楔形文字，其文字属于古埃及人和赫梯人于公元前 13 世纪签订的《卡迭石和平条约》</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:39:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</guid></item><item><title>一只水獭百年来首次回到纽约市布朗克斯河。现在，您可以帮忙命名</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-otter-just-returned-to-new-york-citys-bronx-river-for-the-first-time-in-a-century-now-you-can-help-name-it-180989556/</link><description>今年夏天早些时候，一台追踪相机拍摄了这只动物，这提供了一个充满希望的迹象，表明经过数十年的修复工作，曾经被污染的城市水道正在恢复</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:06:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-otter-just-returned-to-new-york-citys-bronx-river-for-the-first-time-in-a-century-now-you-can-help-name-it-180989556/</guid></item><item><title>科学表明，从促进心理健康到降低痴呆风险，这就是为什么阅读对你非常有益</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-boosting-mental-health-to-reducing-dementia-risk-heres-why-reading-is-extremely-good-for-you-according-to-science-180989548/</link><description>越来越多的证据表明，经常读书可以改善大脑和心理健康，提高读写能力和数学技能，甚至可以减缓认知能力下降。更重要的是，小说似乎还有一个额外的好处，那就是向读者介绍他人的观点</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:33:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-boosting-mental-health-to-reducing-dementia-risk-heres-why-reading-is-extremely-good-for-you-according-to-science-180989548/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下澳大利亚的海豚“泡泡”吧，它会追赶鱼直到它们吐出来，然后吃掉它们吐出来的食物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-bubbles-a-dolphin-in-australia-that-chases-fish-until-they-barf-then-eats-their-upchucked-meals-180989547/</link><description>科学家记录了 11 次 Bubbles 成功以这种方式吃零食的例子。它们标志着对鲸类动物（包括海豚、鲸鱼和鼠海豚在内的海洋哺乳动物）中盗食行为的一些首次详细观察。</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-bubbles-a-dolphin-in-australia-that-chases-fish-until-they-barf-then-eats-their-upchucked-meals-180989547/</guid></item><item><title>通过年度鸟类摄影师大赛的 11 张获奖照片体验鸟类的奇妙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/experience-the-wonder-of-birds-with-these-11-winning-photos-from-the-bird-photographer-of-the-year-contest-180989552/</link><description>从表演交配表演的大鼠尾草到做鬼脸的黄褐色蛙口，这些照片捕捉到了世界鸟类物种令人惊叹的多样性</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:22:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/experience-the-wonder-of-birds-with-these-11-winning-photos-from-the-bird-photographer-of-the-year-contest-180989552/</guid></item><item><title>这位生活在 14 世纪中国的妇女可能因盗窃或通奸而被割掉鼻子</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-woman-who-lived-in-imperial-china-may-have-had-her-nose-cut-off-as-punishment-for-theft-or-adultery-180989551/</link><description>研究人员在她 700 年前的头骨上发现了愈合的迹象，这表明她在痛苦的制裁中幸存下来，甚至可能继续佩戴假肢</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-woman-who-lived-in-imperial-china-may-have-had-her-nose-cut-off-as-punishment-for-theft-or-adultery-180989551/</guid></item><item><title>水星有皱纹，表明它正在收缩。现在，科学家们表示，地球的萎缩程度远远超出了之前的想象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mercury-has-wrinkles-that-show-its-shrinking-now-scientists-say-the-planet-has-shriveled-far-more-than-we-previously-thought-180989532/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，太阳系最小的行星自大约 45 亿年前诞生以来，已经缩小了 30%</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:12:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mercury-has-wrinkles-that-show-its-shrinking-now-scientists-say-the-planet-has-shriveled-far-more-than-we-previously-thought-180989532/</guid></item><item><title>克劳德·莫奈长期隐藏的《鸢尾花》即将成为法国有史以来拍卖的最昂贵的画作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/claude-monets-long-hidden-iris-is-about-to-become-the-most-expensive-painting-ever-auctioned-in-france-180989546/</link><description>该艺